{{define "landing"}}<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Peyva Sandbox</title>
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 24 24'%3E%3Crect width='24' height='24' rx='6' fill='%233b6ef6'/%3E%3Ctext x='12' y='17' font-family='Arial,sans-serif' font-size='14' font-weight='700' fill='white' text-anchor='middle'%3EP%3C/text%3E%3C/svg%3E">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{.AssetPrefix}}styles.css?v={{.StyleVersion}}">
</head>
<body class="landing">
<main class="landing-main">
  <header class="landing-hero">
    <div class="brand">
      <span class="brand-mark large">P</span>
      <div>
        <div class="brand-name">Peyva Sandbox</div>
        <div class="brand-tagline">Learn distributed systems by building one.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h1>Build a wallet. Break it. Fix it. Twenty-two times.</h1>
    <p class="landing-lead">peyva is a small payments system: alice sends bob $20, and the money arrives exactly once. You build it one piece at a time, and each piece exists because the chapter before it showed you a failure.</p>
    <a class="landing-start" href="{{.AssetPrefix}}chapter-0.html">Start with Chapter 0</a>
  </header>

  <section class="landing-how">
    <h2>How a chapter works</h2>
    <ol class="landing-steps">
      <li><b>Read</b> the concepts and why they matter. About a hundred words.</li>
      <li><b>Copy</b> a prompt into your own AI coding assistant. It writes the code, in the language you chose.</li>
      <li><b>Run it</b> and watch it fail the way the chapter said it would. Then fix it.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="landing-note">There is no finished code to download. That is the point: you prompt for it, run it, and see for yourself.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="landing-need">
    <h2>What you need</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>An AI coding assistant. Claude Code, Codex, Copilot, or any other.</li>
      <li>A language. Pick one of {{len .Languages}} in Chapter 0 and keep it for the whole book.</li>
      <li>One laptop. No cloud, no containers, nothing to install to read.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="landing-chapters">
    <h2>The chapters</h2>
    <ol class="landing-list" start="0">
      {{range .Chapters}}<li><a href="{{$.AssetPrefix}}chapter-{{.Number}}.html"><span class="landing-num">{{.Number}}</span> {{.Title}}</a><span class="landing-cat">{{.Category}}</span></li>
      {{end}}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <footer class="landing-foot">
    <a class="landing-start" href="{{.AssetPrefix}}chapter-0.html">Start with Chapter 0</a>
  </footer>
</main>
<script src="{{.AssetPrefix}}app.js?v={{.ScriptVersion}}"></script>
</body>
</html>
{{end}}
